    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on **Corbin Carroll** (87.14) today, as he draws a highly favorable matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+14%) and a strong dynamic platoon advantage, making him our premier start for both raw production and stolen base potential. Joining him at the top of the projected outputs are **Josh Naylor** (73.91) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10), both of whom capitalize on exploitable expected ERAs from Walker Buehler and Tomoyuki Sugano, respectively. **James Wood** (68.90) also earns a high-leverage start out of the leadoff spot; his ability to maximize the +10% order bonus while maintaining a solid 0.378 xwOBA makes him an essential component of today\u2019s pursuit of Runs and SB.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical tradeoffs, most notably the decision to bench **Austin Riley** (51.43). Despite a respectable score, **Austin Riley** narrowly missed the cut due to the superior efficiency of **Vinnie Pasquantino** (65.10) against Leahy, where the latter\u2019s massive +14% platoon advantage created a clear separation in projected production. Meanwhile, the lineup relies heavily on the environment to elevate floor-level players like **Kyle Karros** (61.47), whose score is propped up significantly by a +14% park factor that compensates for his projected #9 spot in the order. \n\nRisk management remains a primary concern as all lineup positions currently rely on assumed batting orders. **Tyler Soderstrom** (56.79) represents our highest-risk play, as his positive park and platoon metrics are sharply offset by the -19% penalty associated with facing Trevor McDonald, an elite arm by xERA standards. Similarly, while **Mickey Moniak** (68.66) grades well, his aggressive platoon penalty (-15%) against Eduardo Rodriguez highlights the fragility of the model should the lineup configurations shift post-publication. Managers should monitor weather updates closely, particularly for those players positioned in stadiums with projected wind-out benefits like **Dalton Rushing** and **Travis Bazzana**.",
